"""
Inolux IN-PI15TAT5R5G5B addressable RGB LED with integrated controller IC.

NeoPixel/SK6812-class single-wire serial protocol (800 kHz, unipolar
zeroing code). 1515 (1.5x1.5 mm), 4-pin top mount. VDD 3.7-5.5 V.
Cascade by wiring DOUT to the next LED's DIN.

Includes a 1 uF 0402 X7R decoupling capacitor between VDD and GND, per
the datasheet's typical application circuit (§Typical Application
Circuit). Place the cap adjacent to pin 2 (VDD) with a tight return to
pin 4 (GND) to suppress switching noise from the integrated PWM drivers
that would otherwise corrupt the 800 kHz data line in long cascades.

For chains of more than a handful of LEDs, the host board should also
add (a) a bulk electrolytic (500-1000 uF, 6.3V+) at the supply entry,
and (b) a 300-500 ohm series resistor on the data line at the first
LED's DIN. Those are board-level concerns and live with the chain head,
not per pixel.
"""

Capacitor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Capacitor.zen")

VDD = io(Power(voltage="3.7V to 5.5V"))
GND = io(Ground)
DIN = io(Net)
DOUT = io(Net)

Component(
    name="IN-PI15TAT5R5G5B",
    symbol=Symbol(library="IN-PI15TAT5R5G5B.kicad_sym"),
    pins={
        "DIN": DIN,
        "VDD": VDD,
        "DOUT": DOUT,
        "GND": GND,
    },
)

Capacitor(name="C_VDD", value="1uF", voltage="10V", package="0402", P1=VDD, P2=GND)

